{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, after Lot parted from him.</b> Not a satisfactory interpretation — if the intention is: walk through what you have apportioned with Lot." "<b>After Lot parted from him.</b> So that Lot would have no claim against Abraham, saying: I am your partner and I shall have a portion with you in the land."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The comment rejects an interpretation that reads the verse as 'go [walk] through what you divided with Lot'; the syntax is elliptic and the reading uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:06.743406135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}